Stores your tier's cards, all of them in one call: the tier's whole target, or what it still needs. Each card that passes is stored and sent to pass 1 of the gate; a card with a fault is refused alone, its every fault named: a title over 120 characters, a canonical title over 160, a summary over 280, a body outside 200 to 1,800, prose over 1,200, a mermaid block that doesn't open with a diagram type, a code block in a topic with no code cards, a fence left open, a passage outside the grounding, a card past the tier's target, more of a form than its quota, or a second hero. An ascii card carries an art request, a gag or an informative drawing within the tier's numbers for each, with what it should show and ideas for drawing it, which designer_toad draws once the card is accepted; no other card has art. A diagram card is a mermaid flowchart with no styling. A card counts as its form whatever else it holds: an ascii card with a code block is an ascii card. The verdicts wake you.
